invariant: INV-16
file: widemul.h
catches: widemul_runtime_test
reason: widemul_p256_fe_sqr inverts its branch, so p256_fe_sqr runs the native
  multiply for every answer but CH_WIDEMUL_CONSTANT_TIME, the unset field
  and CH_WIDEMUL_NOT_STATED among them, and the decomposition for the one
  answer that states the multiply's timing. Every byte still comes out
  the same. bin/widemul_runtime_test counts the calls into each copy and
  requires the native copies alone under the constant-time answer.

--- old
    if (widemul_native(widemul)) {
        p256_fe_sqr_native(o, a);
--- new
    if (!widemul_native(widemul)) {
        p256_fe_sqr_native(o, a);
